  "correctionNote": "Corrected from the Belfast Corporation register of members (PRONI LA/7/1/CA/1/3): Wm. J. Gunning's vote is 3,174 as the register records it (previously 3,194, from the newspaper source). The PRONI register staging (Nov 2026) changed Kenneth Bew's vote to 4,443, as the Belfast Corporation register of members (PRONI LA/7/1/CA/1/3) records it. It is restored to the printed 4,413 (proni-items and council-audit, Nov 2026), read on the page image of the Belfast Telegraph, 21 May 1964, p. 9: the printed majority of 1,101 is Bew's 4,413 less Campbell's 3,312, so the register's 4,443 is a slip of the pen.",
  "note": "Bew's 4,413 is the Belfast Telegraph's figure and the one its printed majority of 1,101 needs (4,413 - 3,312: the paper's majorities are the top elected candidate's lead over the top unsuccessful one); the Belfast Corporation register of members (PRONI LA/7/1/CA/1/3) records 4,443, which would make 1,131."
